    "body": "> I don't think we'd be interested in supporting bringing up the keyboard without user interaction on iOS.\r\n> \r\n> @whsieh\r\n\r\nThis is true, but once the user has already focused an element with user interaction, Safari should allow for the `inputmode` to dynamically change.\r\n\r\nFor instance, if a user taps on a field that has `inputmode=none`, and it changes later to `inputmode=text`, we’ll allow the keyboard to show up.",
