    "updated_at": "2019-09-03T14:42:27Z",
    "body": "Thanks for bringing this up, @rniwa.  Yes, allowing VK changes only with user activation makes perfect sense.  In addition manual focusing as mentioned by @whsieh, I was also thinking that an app can draw a button \"Show virtual keyboard\" when the it makes sense to show one but the platform or the user made it hidden.  Here the change in visibility would only happen once the user taps on the button.\r\n\r\nOne question though: should we have the user activation restriction even for hiding the keyboard (e.g. when changing `inputmode=text` to `inputmode=none`?\r\n",
