    "created_at": "2019-09-03T16:32:03Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-09-03T16:32:03Z",
    "body": "> Can we possibly spec the dynamic change behavior of inputmode to support this use-case?\r\n\r\nFrom my reading of the spec this is currently the behavior; it says \"The user agent should display  virtual keyboard...\" for each state, and states can change.\r\n\r\nWe could add a note explaining this consequences of the current spec, or make it more obvious in some other way.\r\n\r\nHowever, it sounds like what we're now discussing is a proposal to change the spec so that there are two states:\r\n\r\n- The \"real\" inputmode, which can only be changed with user activation\r\n- The state of the inputmode attribute, which is changed via DOM manipulation\r\n\r\nThat's a more involved change, indeed.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/527536791/reactions",
