    "created_at": "2019-09-06T15:32:29Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-09-06T15:32:29Z",
    "body": "Yes, two separate states is a problem.  This is true even when the `inputmode` value is never changed dynamically.  For example, when an `<input inputmode=\"text\">` gets manual focus, the VK appears but the user can still hide the keyboard by pressing the \"back\" button on most smartphones.\r\n\r\nI think a read-only state like `navigator.virtualKeyboardActive = {true, false}` solves this problem.  \r\n\r\n@domenic, would this address your concern?  If yes, I will propose a spec change to highlight the dynamic scenario, and also file a Chrome bug to fix the VK behavior when switching way from `none`.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/528902406/reactions",
