    "body": "I discussed with @mustaqahmed offline briefly, and he clarified his above comment for me. Let me summarize:\r\n\r\n- We should update the spec to reflect that there are two underlying pieces of state:\r\n  - A (global, per-user agent) \"is virtual keyboard showing\" boolean\r\n  - A (per editable element) inputmode enumeration\r\n  - Setting the inputmode to none on the currently focused element will set the \"is virtual keyboard showing\" boolean to false. (No user activation required)\r\n  - Setting the inputmode away from none on the currently focused element will set the \"is virtual keyboard showing\" boolean to true, _only with user activation_.\r\n  - The user agent/user may change the \"is virtual keyboard showing\" boolean in other ways as desired, e.g. the user can use the UI to hide the keyboard\r\n  - Changing the inputmode on the currently focused element should update the virtual keyboard appearance and behavior in the user agent. (The spec currently implies this, but it could definitely be clearer.)\r\n- We can also consider a follow-up proposal to more directly expose the \"is virtual keyboard showing\" boolean to web developers\r\n  - E.g., a read-only `navigator.virtualKeyboardActive`\r\n  - E.g., a `\"virtualkeyboardstatechange\"` event which indicates `navigator.virtualKeyboardActive` has changed",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
