    "created_at": "2019-11-07T16:21:17Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-11-07T16:21:17Z",
    "body": "@snianu: Your point seems logical that the \"type\" of the virtual keyboard and the \"visibility\" of the keyboard are orthogonal ideas.  It's the app's responsibility to define a \"type\", neither the user agent nor the user has any say here.  For \"visibility\", the responsibilities are _kind of_ opposite: the user and the user agent ultimately control it, and the app can only suggest an option.  So a separate `inputPanelPolicy` field makes perfect sense to me, with `inputMode=none` implying a generic/unknown _type_ of keyboard instead of \"no keyboard\".\r\n\r\n@domenic, @rniwa: If you agree this split is reasonable, we would:\r\n- use this issue to cover dynamic VK \"types\", and\r\n- open a new issue for `inputPanelPolicy` to cover \"visibility\" of VK.\r\n\r\nPlease let us know your thoughts.\r\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
